<title>BRAZIL: Telebras second most active foreign stock in US.</title>
<headline>Telebras second most active foreign stock in US.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state telecoms group Telebras shares were the second most actively traded among foreign firms on U.S. stock exchanges in 1996, financial newspaper Gazeta Mercantil said on Monday.</p>
<p>In its first year of trade on the New York Stock Exchange, trade in Telebras was worth $26.8 billion, it said. The first most active foreign company was Royal Dutch Petroleum, with $90 million more.</p>
<p>Gazeta Mercantil also said trades in American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) surged last year, totalling $345 billion, 25 percent more than in 1995.</p>
<p>--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55112485412</p>
